1
00:00:00,231 --> 00:00:03,159
Responsible for reports tells the reviewer little.

2
00:00:03,466 --> 00:00:07,734
A stronger statement identifies the business problem, your own work,

3
00:00:07,899 --> 00:00:11,046
the system involved, and a result you can substantiate.

4
00:00:11,378 --> 00:00:14,564
The goal is clear evidence rather than impressive wording.

5
00:00:15,657 --> 00:00:20,324
For example, explain how you reconciled Sales and Finance definitions,

6
00:00:20,824 --> 00:00:24,951
automated a recurring consolidation, or improved a handoff.

7
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:28,907
Use measured figures only when you have the underlying evidence.

8
00:00:29,214 --> 00:00:32,103
The example achievements in the source are fictional.

9
00:00:33,149 --> 00:00:37,601
SQL, data pipelines, commercial analysis, and process design can help

10
00:00:37,601 --> 00:00:39,964
with migration and Revenue Operations.

11
00:00:40,279 --> 00:00:42,132
They demonstrate relevant reasoning.

12
00:00:42,448 --> 00:00:45,828
They do not by themselves establish hands-on knowledge of Salesforce

13
00:00:45,828 --> 00:00:50,053
sharing, permissions, Flow behavior, or production releases.

14
00:00:51,114 --> 00:00:54,545
If you have not administered production Salesforce, say so.

15
00:00:54,890 --> 00:00:58,034
Show the relevant work you have completed and the support

16
00:00:58,034 --> 00:00:59,300
or learning still needed.

17
00:00:59,632 --> 00:01:04,413
Calling yourself an experienced administrator without that experience creates a

18
00:01:04,413 --> 00:01:05,756
credibility problem.

19
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:12,741
A practice project can show records, relationships, access decisions, automation,

20
00:01:12,882 --> 00:01:15,800
reports, test results, and documentation.

21
00:01:16,124 --> 00:01:19,694
Clearly label it as a learning environment with fictional data.

22
00:01:20,017 --> 00:01:24,147
It strengthens the evidence while remaining different from production ownership.

23
00:01:25,181 --> 00:01:29,759
Connect commercial problems to data, automation, and revenue systems.

24
00:01:30,065 --> 00:01:33,522
Explain what you personally contributed and what the team did.

25
00:01:33,854 --> 00:01:37,491
The source’s individualized career assessment is generalized here;

26
00:01:37,952 --> 00:01:41,857
these lessons do not verify any learner’s background or predict

27
00:01:41,857 --> 00:01:43,032
hiring outcomes.
